-- חוק שכר שווה לעובדת ולעובד, התשנ"ו-1996 — sections 1, 2, 3, 6, 12, 13
-- and 14: that the law means to prevent discrimination between the sexes in
-- pay and in every other remuneration in connection with work; that a woman
-- and a man employed by one employer at one workplace are owed equal pay,
-- and equal other remuneration, for the same work, work equal in substance
-- or work of equal value; what work of equal value is; that a difference
-- the nature of the work requires — output, quality, seniority, training or
-- education, the workplace's location — is allowed where it is no
-- discrimination by sex, and the employer proves it; that the right cannot
-- be conditioned or waived; that a benefit given in connection with birth
-- or parenthood is not taken into account; and that the State is an
-- employer under the law, each ministry a workplace of its own. The text is
-- laws/equal-pay-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים הפתוח;
-- the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: no document of the corpus cites the law, but the
-- instruments give pay and other remuneration, and where one gives it by
-- sex the law is the floor. Who does the same work, how a term written in
-- one sex is read, and what is weighed against §2 where the Equal
-- Opportunities Law's §3(ב) keeps a woman's better right, is convention
-- instruments.equal-pay-teaching, a pick for the lawyer.
--
-- Remuneration is compared as the instruments give it: an amount, or
-- whether a benefit is given at all. The law names no sex-specific
-- figure; it compares what one employee of each sex gets for the same work.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties

§ `חוק שכר שווה לעובדת ולעובד — שכר שווה וגמול אחר שווה`

§§ `1`

-- The law is meant to promote equality and prevent discrimination between
-- the sexes in pay and in every other remuneration in connection with work.
@ref law:1
`the Equal Pay Law reaches every remuneration in connection with work` MEANS TRUE

§§ `2`

-- A woman and a man employed by one employer at one workplace are owed
-- equal pay for the same work, for work equal in substance, or for work of
-- equal value; so too for every other remuneration the employer gives the
-- employee, or for him, in connection with his work. "Other remuneration":
-- every supplement, benefit, allowance, grant, fringe condition, payment
-- for expenses or for keeping a car, use of a telephone, a quota of
-- overtime, professional books, clothing, use of a car, or any other reward
-- in money or money's worth, directly or not, even where it is not wages.
@desc How two jobs compare under sections 2 and 3 of the Equal Pay Law.
DECLARE `how two jobs compare under the Equal Pay Law` IS ONE OF
    `the same work, as the Equal Pay Law compares it`
    `work equal in substance, as the Equal Pay Law compares it`
    `work of equal value, as the Equal Pay Law compares it`
    `work the Equal Pay Law does not set side by side`

@desc What the Equal Pay Law obliges an employer.
DECLARE `Equal Pay Law act` IS ONE OF
    `pay the woman and the man equally and give them equal other remuneration`

@ref law:2
GIVEN `the woman and the man work for one employer at one workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `their jobs` IS A `how two jobs compare under the Equal Pay Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 2 of the Equal Pay Law sets their pay side by side` `the woman and the man work for one employer at one workplace` `their jobs` IF
        `the woman and the man work for one employer at one workplace`
    AND (NOT (`their jobs` EQUALS `work the Equal Pay Law does not set side by side`))

@ref law:2
GIVEN `section 2 sets their pay side by side` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Equal Pay Law act`
DECIDE `equal pay and equal other remuneration under section 2` `section 2 sets their pay side by side` IS
    IF `section 2 sets their pay side by side`
    THEN (PARTY `the employer`
          MUST  `pay the woman and the man equally and give them equal other remuneration`
          LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "Equal Pay Law, section 2: a woman and a man doing the same work, work equal in substance or work of equal value are owed equal pay and equal other remuneration")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Whether what an instrument gives the two meets §2: where §2 sets them
-- side by side, the remuneration is the same — an amount, or a benefit
-- given or not — unless §6 allows the difference or §13 keeps the benefit
-- out of the law.
@ref law:2
GIVEN `section 2 sets their pay side by side` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the woman gets` IS A NUMBER
      `what the man gets` IS A NUMBER
      `section 6 allows the difference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit section 13 keeps out of the law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the remuneration meets section 2 of the Equal Pay Law` `section 2 sets their pay side by side` `what the woman gets` `what the man gets` `section 6 allows the difference` `a benefit section 13 keeps out of the law` IF
        (NOT `section 2 sets their pay side by side`)
    OR  `what the woman gets` EQUALS `what the man gets`
    OR  `section 6 allows the difference`
    OR  `a benefit section 13 keeps out of the law`

-- Where it does not, the one who gets less is owed what the other gets:
-- the law raises the lower, and nothing in it lowers the higher.
@ref law:2
GIVEN `what the woman gets` IS A NUMBER
      `what the man gets` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what section 2 of the Equal Pay Law owes each of them` `what the woman gets` `what the man gets` IS
    max `what the woman gets` `what the man gets`

#ASSERT `the remuneration meets section 2 of the Equal Pay Law` TRUE 100 100 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the remuneration meets section 2 of the Equal Pay Law` TRUE 100 90 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the remuneration meets section 2 of the Equal Pay Law` TRUE 100 90 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the remuneration meets section 2 of the Equal Pay Law` TRUE 100 90 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the remuneration meets section 2 of the Equal Pay Law` FALSE 100 90 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `what section 2 of the Equal Pay Law owes each of them` 90 100 EQUALS 100

§§ `3`

-- Work is of equal value to another, though not the same or equal in
-- substance, where the two weigh the same — among other things in the
-- skills, effort, expertise and responsibility they require and in the
-- surroundings they are done in.
@desc What section 3 of the Equal Pay Law weighs two jobs by.
DECLARE `what section 3 of the Equal Pay Law weighs` HAS
    `the skills required`       IS A NUMBER
    `the effort required`       IS A NUMBER
    `the expertise required`    IS A NUMBER
    `the responsibility borne`  IS A NUMBER
    `the surroundings of the work` IS A NUMBER

@ref law:3
GIVEN a IS A `what section 3 of the Equal Pay Law weighs`
      b IS A `what section 3 of the Equal Pay Law weighs`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `of equal value under section 3 of the Equal Pay Law` a b IF
        a's `the skills required` EQUALS b's `the skills required`
    AND a's `the effort required` EQUALS b's `the effort required`
    AND a's `the expertise required` EQUALS b's `the expertise required`
    AND a's `the responsibility borne` EQUALS b's `the responsibility borne`
    AND a's `the surroundings of the work` EQUALS b's `the surroundings of the work`

§§ `6`

-- (א): §2 does not prevent a difference in pay or other remuneration the
-- character or nature of the work requires — output, quality, seniority,
-- training or education, the workplace's location — where it is no
-- discrimination by sex. (ב): where the court finds the jobs the same,
-- equal in substance or of equal value, the employer who claims such a
-- reason proves it.
@desc A reason section 6(א) of the Equal Pay Law names for a difference in pay.
DECLARE `a reason section 6 of the Equal Pay Law names` IS ONE OF
    `the output of the work`
    `the quality of the work`
    `seniority in the work`
    `training or education`
    `the workplace's location`
    `another requirement of the work's character or nature`
    `the employee's sex, or a status that stands for it`

@ref law:6
GIVEN `the reason for the difference` IS A `a reason section 6 of the Equal Pay Law names`
      `the employer proved it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 6(ב)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6 of the Equal Pay Law allows the difference` `the reason for the difference` `the employer proved it` IF
        `the employer proved it`
    AND (NOT (`the reason for the difference` EQUALS `the employee's sex, or a status that stands for it`))

#ASSERT `section 6 of the Equal Pay Law allows the difference` `seniority in the work` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 6 of the Equal Pay Law allows the difference` `seniority in the work` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 6 of the Equal Pay Law allows the difference` `the employee's sex, or a status that stands for it` TRUE

§§ `12`

-- An employee's right under the law cannot be conditioned or waived: an
-- instrument that gives less does not take it away.
@ref law:12
`a right under the Equal Pay Law cannot be conditioned or waived` MEANS TRUE

§§ `13`

-- A benefit given to an employee in connection with birth or parenthood is
-- not taken into account for the law.
@ref law:13
GIVEN `a benefit given in connection with birth or parenthood` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 13 of the Equal Pay Law keeps the benefit out` `a benefit given in connection with birth or parenthood` IF
    `a benefit given in connection with birth or parenthood`

§§ `14`

-- The law reaches the State as an employer, but (1) each ministry, as §1 of
-- the State Service (Appointments) Law defines one, is a workplace of its
-- own; (2) the Ministers may make a unit, or several, of one ministry a
-- workplace of its own by order.
@ref law:14
`the Equal Pay Law reaches the State as an employer` MEANS TRUE

@ref law:14
GIVEN `in the same ministry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order makes their units separate workplaces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 14(2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `one State workplace under section 14 of the Equal Pay Law` `in the same ministry` `an order makes their units separate workplaces` IF
        `in the same ministry`
    AND (NOT `an order makes their units separate workplaces`)

#ASSERT `one State workplace under section 14 of the Equal Pay Law` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `one State workplace under section 14 of the Equal Pay Law` FALSE FALSE
